today during the Game Developers  Conference AMD announced the Radeon Pro  duo which they're calling the world's  first content creation platform aimed  squarely at the VR developer this takes  the form of a dual GPU featuring two  fury x class graphics cards running side  by side making it absolutely the most  powerful graphics card in the world by  far that's the description  AMD marketing executive Chris hook used  to explain the new board which is  principally focused on virtual reality  rather than just doing another  workstation card we actually started  about a year ago we sampled VR  developers about what they'd like to see  from a VR card  he said AMD wondered what would happen  if we took professional workstation  class drivers and gaming drivers and  fuse them together to create a platform  that would not only give you great  scaling across previz and post rendering  platforms but would also be a great  gaming platform the answer is the Radeon  Pro duo dual GPU for VR specifically the  fact that it has two distinct graphic  chips on one card will help reduce  latency a key point for VR developers  AMD is investing so heavily in VR  because it sees a future beyond gaming  alone the company has already formed a  partnership with the associate press for  a newsgathering VR app whilst it's  partnered with Fox Studios for a VR  experience based on the upcoming  Assassin's Creed film that hits this  winter AMD is also working with the  Smithsonian for a VR app that will take  you to the dunes of Kitty Hawk North  Carolina where the white brothers took  their first flights this Radium pro duo  also makes use of AMD's liquid VR  framework while it boasts an incredible  16 teraflops of compute performance it's  coming early quarter to 2016 and will  carry a price tag of $1,500 so will you  be picking up the shiny new card for  your VR machine let us know in the  comment section below and for all the  technical specifics of the radium pro 2  oh and all the news from GDC keep tuned  in to GameSpot calm
 

